.TH KSPKAN 1 2026-11-24 "kspkan 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
kspkan \- small mod manager for Kerbal Space Program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kspkan
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ command " [" args ]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kspkan
installs, removes and upgrades Kerbal Space Program mods using the
CKAN module list (CKAN-meta).  It resolves dependencies (depends,
any_of, provides, conflicts), offers recommended and suggested mods,
checks every download against its SHA-256 or SHA-1 sum, and records
each file it installs, so that removal deletes exactly those files.
.PP
With no command it opens a full screen mode; press
.B ?
there for the keys.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B update
Fetch the module list.
.TP
.BI search " [query]"
List modules.  Words are ANDed; a leading \- excludes a word.  Also:
.IR author:x " " tag:x " " license:x " " needs:x " " dl>5k " " dl<100
.IR after:2024-01-01 " " before:... " " size<5 " (MB) "
.IR is:installed " " is:update " " is:new " and "
.IR sort:pop | new | small | big | name .
.TP
.BI show " id"
Describe a module.
.TP
.B list
Installed modules.
.TP
.BI install " id[=version] ..."
Install modules and what they need.  Recommended and suggested modules
are offered for choosing.
.TP
.BI remove " id ..."
Remove modules, the modules that need them, and dependencies nothing
needs any more.
.TP
.BI upgrade " [id ...]"
Upgrade installed modules (all of them when none is named).
.TP
.B autoremove
Remove dependencies nothing needs.
.TP
.B clean
Delete downloaded archives.
.TP
.BI add " name [gamedir]"
Remember a game folder (the folder that holds GameData) as an instance.
.TP
.BR instances ", " use " \fIname\fR, " forget " \fIname\fR"
List, choose or forget instances.  Forgetting never touches the game.
.TP
.B version
Print the version.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " name"
Use that instance (default: the last one used).
.TP
.BI \-g " dir"
Use that game folder directly.
.TP
.BI \-k " version"
The game version, when it cannot be read from the game folder.
.TP
.B \-a
Ignore game version compatibility.
.TP
.B \-t
Allow testing and development releases.
.TP
.B \-f
Overwrite files that kspkan did not install.
.TP
.B \-y
Do not ask for confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-S
Also install recommended (\-R), or recommended and suggested (\-S)
modules, without asking.
.TP
.B \-p
List the most downloaded first.
.TP
.B \-m
No colours on the screen.
.TP
.BI \-r " url"
Another module list archive.
.TP
.BI \-s " dir"
Keep all of kspkan's files in dir (used by the tests).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/kspkan
(or
.IR ~/.local/share/kspkan )
.BR instances :
the remembered game folders;
.BR index ", " summary ", " provides ", " counts ", " meta/ :
the module list;
.BR cache/ :
downloads;
.BI inst/ name /installed :
what was installed into each instance.  All are plain text.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set, the screen has no colours.
.TP
.BR ALL_PROXY ", " HTTPS_PROXY
Passed on to curl, which does the downloading.
.SH NOTES
Downloads are done by running
.BR curl (1).
Nothing else is contacted, and kspkan sends nothing about you or your
game anywhere.
